> ### * create_start_level_data
> 
> flush(stderr()); flush(stdout())
> 
> ### Name: create_start_level_data
> ### Title: Generate starting antibody levels
> ### Aliases: create_start_level_data
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> ## Not run: 
> ##D ## Use the minimum of the earliest measurements for each individual and biomarker.
> ##D ## For discrete data, the TRUE calls below randomize the result between its
> ##D ## floor and floor + 1; the FALSE calls retain the summary value.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"min",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"min",TRUE)
> ##D ## Use the maximum of the earliest measurements.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"max",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"max",TRUE)
> ##D ## Use the mean of the earliest measurements.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"mean",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"mean",TRUE)
> ##D ## Use the median of the earliest measurements.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"median",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"median",TRUE)
> ##D ## An unrecognised summary sets starting levels to zero.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"other",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"other",TRUE)
> ##D ## Draw starting levels uniformly between the observed minimum and maximum
> ##D ## for each biomarker group.
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"full_random",FALSE)
> ##D create_start_level_data(example_antibody_data,"full_random",TRUE)
> ## End(Not run)
> 
> 
